 is providing or supervising peer  recovery  support services that uh that bill  foundation for recovering recovery  advocacy project have been so  just integrated in since the beginning  and have have moved the ball forward on  that where  we've got uh that bill the policy has  already been approved  now it's in it what's called a money  committee and  that is just um any bill  that has any financial component to it  after the policy is approved it has to  go through that committee and so that's  where  that bill sits now another bill that  sits in a money committee is assembly  bill 370  that's assemblywoman dickman's bill on  allocating some of the liquor tax  revenue  for recovery services so we're seeing  again just some of that money diverted  from the general fund  specific to recovery services  um and then we've also got um i'm sure  many of you have seen in the news  some of the opioid litigation uh  that have uh infused some money into the  attorney general's office  after having uh battled some of those  pharmaceutical companies 45 million  dollars is one of the latest settlements  so senate bill 390 is senator ratty's  bill  that will focus on the administration of  that uh  that opioid litigation funding and  um and her bill also will uh use part of  that for the creation of a statewide  behavioral health  crisis hotline so that bill also sitting  in a money  committee as you can imagine but um  we will be providing to anna maria and  the rest of the team  a recovery update that you'll see or  sorry recovery  friendly legislative update that you'll  see um  sent out probably later in the week and  we'll have links to all the bills so you  can  dive in as deep as you want you can read  them and we are always  happy and available to um answer  questions and  just help walk anyone that's interested  through the process so you can  see where we are because as trey said  120 days  goes by very quickly and if it weren't  for these deadlines it would be pretty