ilding communities of recovery program  and he is also a peer recovery support  specialist at foundation for recovery  and we have walter sanders from rural  nevada counseling  so welcome everyone uh thank you for  being here today  so let's go ahead and just hop right in  i have a few questions that i want to  open up to the full panel  um would each of you mind going around  and sharing a little bit about your  organization's work and what you do in  the community  and bob we could go ahead and start with  you  hello everybody thank you sean so much  my name is bob victory uh  and as mentioned i am a project  coordinator with pact coalition i'm also  a person in long-term recovery and  i wish i had all the time in the world  to express the gratitude and hope that i  have heard here today it is just  incredibly it has infused me with just  incredible energy to do this good work  and i thank everybody  uh so for those of you many of us uh  participants and stakeholders of packed  coalition are on the call today  so i'll do my best to be brief about who  uh we are in the community  but we are um a coalition for a safe  and drug-free community and we're a  non-profit 501c3  and i think the most important thing i  can say about pac is that i've  discovered since i've been  on the team is that we bring community  organizations  leadership um agencies  together to strengthen the community by  acting as a neutral convening table and  that's a  a term that jamie ross has you know  impressed upon me our executive director  so when i'm out representing the  community it was mentioned  we are nonpartisan we bring together  over 70  organizations and agencies together  around the table every month  we used to do it in person we hope to do  it soon  and uh we work to address emergent  issues around substance misuse  by offering resources of prevention  we're a pass-through agency for federal  and state funding  and our work is to get these resources  out to the agencies that ar